pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Date Added</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">?</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"Status\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Status</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Obtainable</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\n\t</section>\n\n\n\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span></h2>\n<p>The <b>Ash Tree</b> takes on a unique appearance, having an irregularly shaped, burnt-black trunk and no leaves.\n</p><p>The tree appears pitch black while in the cave, but is actually a bit brighter than refined <a href=\"/wiki/Blackstone\" title=\"Blackstone\">blackstone</a>.\nThe tree can be used in schematics like every other material in-game. Its logs are ideal for use in builds that involve ash or dark materials.  \n</p><p>The Ash Tree, same as <a href=\"/wiki/Magma_Tree\" title=\"Magma Tree\">Magma Tree</a>, can be found inside the <a href=\"/wiki/Magma_Caves\" title=\"Magma Caves\">Magma Cave</a> and at a <a href=\"/wiki/Meteor_Core\" title=\"Meteor Core\">Meteor Crash</a>. Additionally, any tree can be turned into an Ash Tree if a player ignites one using the <a href=\"/wiki/Flamethrower\" title=\"Flamethrower\">Flamethrower</a>, however, these trees sell for the same price as the original tree it came from. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trivia\">Trivia</span></h2>\n<ul><li>The <a href=\"/wiki/Deadwood\" title=\"Deadwood\">Deadwood</a> tree is called 'AshTree' when used in a schematic, but is in fact a completely different tree and should not be confused with the true Ash tree.</li></ul>\n<table class=\"navbox mw-collapsible\" style=\"background:#291F1D; width:100%; padding:.1em; margin:.5em auto; -webkit-border-radius:5px; -moz-border-radius:0 10px 10px 0\" data-expandtext